# Hide on the Ceiling is an instant: in Bot2's turn, with Lightning Bolt aimed at Bot1's Ornithopter on the stack, Bot1 exiles the Ornithopter with X = 1
# ({1}{U}). The Bolt's target is gone when it resolves, so it is countered (CR 608.2b) and deals no damage. The Ornithopter returns at the beginning of
# that turn's end step, Bot2's: a new object under Bot1's control, still Bot1's.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Ornithopter
Hide on the Ceiling
Plains x3
Plains x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Plains x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Hide on the Ceiling.Cast(X: 1)
Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Exile = Ornithopter
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main2]
? Bot1.Life = 20
? Exile = Ornithopter
[T2 Bot2.End]
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Exile.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Sapphire; Mox Jet; Ornithopter
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
Bot1.Graveyard = Hide on the Ceiling
